      "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $x=2{y}^{3}-{y}^{4}$ and the $y$-axis. What integral gives the volume of the solid generated when that region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?",
      "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{y}^{3}-{y}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {y}^{3}(2-y) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $y=0,\\,2.$ So, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=2.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{c}^{d}yf(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}y(2{y}^{3}-{y}^{4})\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$",
